Description: Offer the draft session management protocol next to the final one.
 xdg-session-management.patch renames mutter's session management protocol from its draft name,
 xx_session_manager_v1, to the final xdg_session_manager_v1, as mutter 51 does. Chromium, up to at least 156,
 speaks only the draft, behind its WaylandSessionManagement feature, so it would lose session management with
 that patch alone. This offers the draft again, as a second global next to the final one, served by the same code
 and backed by the same stored sessions. Each session records the protocol it was created through, for the
 interfaces, error codes and events which differ between the two. For the draft, add_toplevel refuses only a
 name in use by a toplevel of the same session object, as mutter 50.1 did and as Chromium was written against.
 Mutter 50.1 offered the draft only with MUTTER_DEBUG_SESSION_MANAGEMENT_PROTOCOL=1, this offers it to every
 client.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-03
